          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            may be thought of as a generalized
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+space"} locally connected space
            %li
              %p
                locally 2-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
                space
            %li
              %p etc. …
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+contractible+space"} locally contractible space
          %p
            have analogs for
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong locally connected topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+n-connected+%28n%2C1%29-topos"} locally n-connected (n,1)-topos
            %li
              %p etc. …
          %h2#definition Definition
          #ConnectedObject.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+object"} connected object
              if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}\big(A, -\big)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+coproduct"} finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            %p
              Equivalently, an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is connected if it is non-empty (in that it is not
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              of two nonempty
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is called a
              %strong locally connected topos
              if every object is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+objects"} connected objects
              (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConnectedObject"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{E}
              there exists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big\{A_i \in \mathcal{E}\big\}_{i \in I}
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\coprod_{i \in I} A_i
                    \\,.
          %p
            If this is the case, it follows that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+set"} index
            set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is unique up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi I
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_0(A) \;\coloneqq\; I
                  \\,.
          %p
            This construction defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℰ
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi Set
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Pi_0 \colon &amp; \mathcal{E} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Set
                  \\\
                  \&amp; A &amp;\mapsto&amp; \pi_0(A)
                  }
          %p
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+sheaf"} locally constant sheaf
            functor, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            part of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
          %p
            This is the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong connected component functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            assigns the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            of that space. See the
            %a{:href => "#Examples"} examples
            below.
          %p
            In summary, for a locally connected topos the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+geometric+morphism"} terminal geometric morphism
            extends to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
