          %p
            The following proposition asserts that the existence of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
            already characterizes locally connected toposes.
          #LocalConnectednessByEssentialGeometricMorphism.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is locally connected precisely if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma : \mathcal{E} \to Set
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential geometric morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi L
                      %mi Const
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Pi_0 \dashv L Const \dashv \Gamma) : \mathcal{E} \to Set
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p The “only if”-case was just claimed/argued above, we need to show the “if”-case.
            %p
              Hence suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi LConst
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Pi_0 \dashv LConst)
              exists. We will show that then every object is a coproduct of connected objects. (A proof also appears as (
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, Lemma C.3.3.6
              ).)
            %p
              First we claim that an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is connected in the
              %a{:href => "#ConnectedObject"} above sense
              precisely if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0(A) = \ast
            %p To see this, observe that
            #eq:EmptyShapeImpliesInitialObject.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∅
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi LConst
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∅
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                    %mo ∅
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∅
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Pi_0(A) \;\simeq\; \varnothing
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    LConst \Pi_0(A) \;\simeq\; \varnothing
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    A \xrightarrow{\eta_{A}} \varnothing
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    A \;\simeq\; \varnothing
                    \\,,
            %p
              where we used that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi LConst
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LConst
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              and that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints+preserve+colimits"} left adjoints preserve colimits
              (
              %a{:href => "initial+object#InitialObjectIsEmptyColimit"} hence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+colimit"} preserve
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+objects"} initial objects
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              in any topos is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+initial+object"} strict
            %p But this gives
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is connected
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Pi_0(A) \simeq \ast
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    A \;\text{is connected}
                    \\,,
            %p
              because if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              as on the left were the coproduct of non-initial
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0(A)
              would be the coproduct of non-initial
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0(A_1)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0(A_2)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:EmptyShapeImpliesInitialObject"} (1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0(A) \simeq \ast
            %p Conversely, to see
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is connected
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \;\text{is connected}
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Pi_0(A) \simeq \ast
            %p observe that the connectivity assumption implies in particular that
            #eq:ASequenceOfIsos.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi LConst
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mi S
                      %mo *
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mi S
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi LConst
                      %mo *
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi S
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Set
                    \\big(
                    \\Pi_0(A)
                    ,\,
                    S
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathcal{E}
                    \\left(
                    A,\,
                    LConst
                    \\coprod_S
                    \\ast
                    \\right)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathcal{E}
                    \\left(
                    A
                    ,\,
                    \\coprod_S \,  LConst \ast
                    \\right)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    {\coprod}_S
                    \\,
                    \\mathcal{E}
                    \\big(
                    A
                    ,\,
                    \\ast
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\coprod_S \ast
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    S
                    \\,,
            %p
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Set
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi LConst
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big(\Pi_0 \dashv LConst\big)
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "adjoint+functor#InTermsOfHomIsomorphism"} hom isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0(A)
              is connected as an object of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+set"} singleton set
            %p With this equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is connected
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \; \text{is connected}
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\Pi_0(A) \simeq \ast
            %p
              in hand (given the extra left adjoint
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is a coproduct of objects for which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0(-)
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} point
            %p
              For that purpose consider for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{E}
              the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi i
                              %mi A
                              %mo *
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Π
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi A
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mphantom
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo −
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo −
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Π
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi A
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo −
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi A
                                %mphantom
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo −
                          %mtd
                            %mi LConst
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    i_A^* {\underset{\underset{\Pi_0(A)}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim}} \ast
                    \&amp;\xrightarrow{\phantom{----}}&amp;
                    {\underset{\underset{\Pi_0(A)}{\longrightarrow}}{lim}} \ast
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\simeq}}\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\big\downarrow{}^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                    \\\
                    A
                    \&amp;\xrightarrow{\phantom{--}i_A\phantom{--}}&amp;
                    LConst \Pi_0 (A)
                    \\,,
                    }
            %p
              where the bottom morphism is the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Π
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi L
                      %mi Const
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Pi \dashv L Const)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
              and the right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              is the identification of any set as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              (here:
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "pullback#PullbackPreservesMonomorphisms"} here
            %p
              Now, by the fact that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              has “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimits"}> universal colimits
              ”, this left morphism is equivalently
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi Π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo *
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo −
                        %mo ∼
                        %mphantom
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo −
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{
                    \\underset{s \in \Pi_0(A)}{\longrightarrow}
                    }{\lim}
                    (i_A^* \ast_s)
                    \\xrightarrow{\phantom{--}\sim\phantom{--}}
                    A
            %p
              and hence expresses
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              as a coproduct of objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi i
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mo *
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_A^* *_s
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi i
                              %mi A
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mo *
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mphantom
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo −
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo −
                          %mtd
                            %mi LConst
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi s
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo −
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi A
                                %mphantom
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo −
                          %mtd
                            %mi LConst
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 0
                            %mi A
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    i_A^* \ast_s &amp;\xrightarrow{\phantom{----}}&amp; LConst *
                    \\\
                    \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow{}^{\mathrlap{s}}
                    \\\
                    A &amp;\xrightarrow{\phantom{--}i_A\phantom{--}}&amp; LConst \Pi_0 A
                    \\,,
                    }
            %p
              where the right morphism includes the element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              into the set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0 A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
              to this diagram and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              on the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi L
                      %mi Const
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Pi_0 \dashv L Const)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
              we get
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi i
                              %mi A
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mo *
                              %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mphantom
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo −
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo −
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 0
                            %mi LConst
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mphantom
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo −
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo −
                                %msub
                                  %mi Π
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mphantom
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo −
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 0
                            %mi LConst
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 0
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mphantom
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo −
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo −
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 0
                            %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Pi_0(i_A^* *_s)
                    \&amp;\xrightarrow{\phantom{-----}}&amp;
                    \\Pi_0 LConst \ast &amp;\xrightarrow{\phantom{---}}&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow^{} &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Pi_0(A)
                    \&amp;\xrightarrow{\phantom{--}\Pi_0(i_A)\phantom{--}}&amp;
                    \\Pi_0 LConst \Pi_0 A
                    \&amp;\xrightarrow{\phantom{----}}&amp;
                    \\Pi_0 A
                    }
            %p
              and by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag+identity"} zig-zag identity
              the bottom morphism is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 0
                            %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi i
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mo *
                        %mi s
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ∼
                      %mi A
                      %mo )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 0
                            %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi i
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mo *
                        %mi s
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ∼
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Pi_0
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{\underset{\Pi_0 A}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\;
                    i_A^* \ast_s
                    \\xrightarrow{\sim}
                    A
                    \\right)
                    \\simeq
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{\underset{\Pi_0 A}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\;
                    \\Pi_0\big(i_A^* \ast_s\big)
                    \\xrightarrow{\sim}
                    \\Pi_0(A)
                    \\right)
            %p
              all the component maps out of the coproduct factor through the point. This means that this can only be an isomorphism if all these component maps are point inclusions, hence if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo *
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0(i_A^* *_s) \simeq *
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in \Pi_0 A
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Beware that Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalConnectednessByEssentialGeometricMorphism"}
              only applies to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+geometric+morphisms"} terminal geometric morphisms
              (of locally connected toposes). The analogous “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+point+of+view"}> relative
              ” characterization of more general
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+geometric+morphisms"} locally connected geometric morphisms
              involves more than just the existence of the extra left adjoint functor, see
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "locally+connected+geometric+morphism#Definition"} there
            %p
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#characterization_over_locally_connected_sites Characterization over locally connected sites
          %p
            See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+site"} locally connected site
          %h3#equivalent_conditions Equivalent conditions
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+categories"} cartesian closed categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
              that preserves
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+functor"} cartesian closed functor
              if the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F(B^A) \to (F(B))^{F(A)}
            %p
              (which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(A) \times F(B^A) \simeq F(A \times B^A) \to F(B)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-functor" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+sheaf"} constant sheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{E}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+functor"} cartesian closed functor
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is a locally connected topos.
          %h3#Connected Locally connected and connected
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topos"} connected topos
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mi Const
                  %mo :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L Const : Set \to E
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \colon E\to Set
              is a locally connected topos, then it is also a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topos"} connected topos
              — in that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi Const
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L Const
              is full and faithful — if and only if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi Const
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L Const
              preserves the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, C3.3.3
            ).
          %p Notice that for a connected and locally connected topos, the adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 0
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Set \stackrel{\overset{\Pi_0}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow} E
          %p
            exhibits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            as being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            at those morphisms that induce isomorphisms of connected components.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          #LocallyConnectedTopologicalSpace.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X) \coloneqq Sh(Op(X))
              is a locally connected topos precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+space"} locally connected space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
              sends a sheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in Sh(X)
              to the set of connected components of the corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+space"} etale space
          #SmoothSpaces.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(CartSp)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spaces"} smooth spaces
              is locally connected. An arbitrary
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Sh(CartSp)
              is sent to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi lim
                        %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_\to X \in Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
              or even a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
          #LCC.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              Every locally connected geometric morphism is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+functor"} locally cartesian closed functor
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              Suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              such that constant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
              exists and is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              functor: if we write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L : PSh(C) \to Sh(C)
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi L
                    %mi Const
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi L
                    %mi Const
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Const
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{Sh(C)}(X, L Const S)
                    \\simeq
                    Hom_{PSh(C)}(X, L Const S)
                    \\simeq
                    Hom_{PSh(C)}(X, Const S)
                    \\simeq
                    Hom_{Set}(\lim_\to X, S)
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular, this is the case if every covering
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is connected, i.e.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+site"} locally connected site
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              furthermore has a terminal object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma\colon Sh(C)\to Set
              (the right adjoint of
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mi Const
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L Const
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi L
                    %mi Const
                    %mi S
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi L
                    %mi Const
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to \Gamma L Const S \cong L Const S(1)
              is an isomorphism. Thus in this case
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              is additionally
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topos"} connected
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C=CartSp
              in example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSpaces"}
              above.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a category with all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              and if the unique functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon C \to \ast
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover-preserving+functor"} cover-preserving functor
              (for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
              equipped with the trivial topology/
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"}> coverage
              ) then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              is locally connected. (In particular, this holds for presheaf toposes). This is because the inclusion of the terminal object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon \ast \to C
              provides a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
              of functors on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+categories"} presheaf categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo !
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi π
                      %mo *
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo *
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi π
                      %mo !
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Ran
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↔
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Set
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\pi_! \simeq Lan_\pi)
                    \\dashv
                    (\pi^\ast \simeq i_! \simeq Lan_i)
                    \\dashv
                    (\pi_\ast \simeq i^\ast )
                    \\dashv
                    (\pi^! \simeq i_* \simeq Ran_i)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    PSh(C) \leftrightarrow PSh(\ast) \simeq Sh(C) \simeq Set
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan_{(-)}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ran
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ran_{(-)}
              denote let and right
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to \ast
              indeed preserves covers and using that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to \ast
              trivially preserves finite limits and hence is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+functor"} flat functor
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+sites"} morphism of sites
              the first three functors here descend to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
              and hence exhibit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              as being locally connected.
            %p
              But
              %strong beware
              that the assumptions here are stronger than they may seem: that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to \ast
              preserves covers is not automatic, but is a strong condition. It is violated as soon as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              contains an empty object with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
              cover, such as is the case in most categories of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+open+subsets"} categories of open subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Op(X)
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyConnectedTopologicalSpace"}
